{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1348821-peach-telepathy-charms","id":1348821,"title":"[PEACH] Telepathy charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-16T03:10:23-08:00","id":1348821,"title":"[PEACH] Telepathy charms","content":"One of my players, whose character is a Zenith monk, asked for some kind of telepathy. I know that this is not <i>exactly </i>the aesthetics of Exalted, but after a while I decided that it might indeed be a funny idea an that it is not as far from Solar themes as one can initially think. Namely, very often telepathy is portrayed as ostensibly not magic <i>per se</i> but rather a feat which can be achieved by raising one's focus and concentration to its peak. <div align=\"left\"><b>Mind Over Matter</b><br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Integrity 4, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Apocryphal<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Mind-cleansing Prana<br /> <br /> With mind as clear as the surface of a lake, the Lawgiver no longer has to struggle with the bonds of matter, once she reaches understanding that bonds are not.<br /> <br /> While the prerequsite is active, after at least five minutes of undisturbed meditation, the Solar is able to move objects with the power of her mind. She can manipulate physical objects up to [Essence \u00d7 20] metres from her using [Perception + Integrity] as her dicepool for Feats of Strength with [Solar\u2019s Integrity] as her Strength rating.<br /> <br /> Whenever precision of the manipulation is relevant, the Unyielding uses the same dice pools as with the actual physical manipulation. For instance, opening a lock usually requires a [Larceny + Dexterity] test. The moves generated by this charm are graceful and tranquil like the Lawgiver herself and generally cannot be used to make attacks without a stunt.<br /> <br /> When the prerequisite is used in conjunction with Clear Mind Discipline, the time required to activate this charm is reduced to a handful of seconds which possibly allows to make appropriate gambits in fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Smite of Focused Will</b><br /> Cost: 4m 3i or 6m, 1wp, 3i<br /> Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 2<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Apocryphal, Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Mind Over Matter, Clear Mind Discipline<br /> <br /> Always focused and looking within the innermost self, the Unyielding strikes with a precise and focused thrust breaking planks and bricks with her clear mind like a martial artist with her fist.<br /> <br /> This charm allows the Lawgiver to make a withering or decisive [Perception + Integrity] attack up to Short range using stats of a light artifact thrown weapon with the Bashing tag. If this attack inflicts at least 3 levels of withering or any amount of decisive damage, the enemy is knocked prone.<br /> <br /> Once per scene, by paying 6m, 1 wp, 3i this charm can be activated reflexively. This can be reset by surviving at least three attacks from a nontrivial foe.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+, this charm can be repurchased. The foes which are knocked prone can be additionally knocked one range band away. Additionally, upon repurchase, the charm can be used to throw objects within medium range with significant power up to one range band. The dicepool for throwing is [Dexterity + Thrown] with Integrity replacing Strength and weapon stats depending on the object thrown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gale From The Clearest Sky </b><br /> Cost: 1wp, 8m<br /> Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Apocryphal, Dual<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Smite of Focused Will<br /> <br /> Unshaken by the surrounding chaos, the Lawgiver draws the power from her uttermost balance, not from fury. Perfectly calm, she strikes her foes with a powerful gale of pure will.<br /> <br /> This charm generates a [Perception + Integrity] withering or decisive attack against an enemy up to medium range from the Lawgiver and (optionally) all enemies within his Close range, using stats of light artifact thrown weapon and Bashing tag. If the attack is withering, only the most successful damage roll grants the Solar Initiative points, but the Exalt gets two points of Initiative for every enemy successfully hit by the attack. If the attack is decisive, the Lawgiver divides her Initiative evenly between foes, adding one additional die of decisive damage for each enemy struck.<br /> <br /> All enemies successfully hit with the attack are knocked prone. If an enemy suffers at least 3 points of Initiative damage or any decisive damage, he is additionally knocked away one range band. At Essence 4+, if an enemy suffers at least 5 points of initiative damage or any decisive damage, he is knocked away two range bands and suffers additional 3 levels of bashing falling damage. All the enemies are knocked away in the same direction. Alternatively, the Lawgiver can attack all characters within her close range in which case they are knocked away radially with the Exalt as the origin.<br /> <br /> <b>Size Matters Not</b><br /> Cost: 3m/1 dot, 1wp<br /> Mins: Integrity 4, Essence 3<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Apocryphal<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Mind over Matter<br /> <br /> Meditating on misleading appearance of things tangible, the Lawgiver breaks the chains restraining her will and lifts boulders like pebbles.<br /> <br /> For every 3m spent, this charm raises Integrity by one, increasing the rating for the purposes of meeting strength requirements in Feats of Strength. The Lawgiver can increase her Integrity at most by [her Essence]. The dice coming from raised Integrity count as charm dice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mind Raises Mountain</b><br /> Cost: 12m, 2wp<br /> Mins: Integrity 5, Essence 5<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keywords: Perilous, Apocryphal<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Size Matters Not<br /> <br /> The Lawgiver is the paragon of the principles by which she lives. She stands still exactly where she should. It is the world that has to move under her unyielding will. She tears down mountain ranges, lifts mighty fleets to the sky, cracks walls of ancient castles, and crushes haughty towers with the power of her inner balance.<br /> <br /> This charm allows the Lawgiver to perform tremendous fiat-level feats of strength involving objects hundreds meters large. Objects manipulated must be within [Essence] miles from her and clearly visible. This generally does not require any roll, but if precision is an issue, the Storyteller might call for it.<br /> <br /> This charm may be used once per story, unless reset by upholding a defining principle against legendary obstacles.</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13416-lanic","name":"Lanic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}